\subsection{Reliability and optimisation}

The reliability picture of Section~\ref{sec:results} recurs here. Multiscale
AKDE-M produced $\bfLargeMultiscaleAkde$ large-error fits
($\bfLargeFracMultiscaleAkde\%$, worst $\bfWorstMultiscaleAkde\times$ its cell
median, all three at $r=1$, $N=5000$ and all three at the smallest penalty
on the grid); the single-scale ablation produced $\bfLargeSingleScaleAkde$
($\bfLargeFracSingleScaleAkde\%$, worst $\bfWorstSingleScaleAkde\times$),
which is what separates its means from its medians in
Table~\ref{tab:bf-results}; SPADES-simplex and the Sheather--Jones estimator
produced none, Abramson one and the EM mixture four. The lower end of the
penalty grid was selected in $\bfLamEdgeMultiscaleAkde\%$ of AKDE-M fits and
$\bfLamEdgeSingleScaleAkde\%$ of single-scale fits.

The first-stage solver is the one deployed in Section~\ref{sec:results} and
it has not been changed, so the optimisation limitation of
Section~\ref{sec:limitations} applies unchanged. Re-deriving the KKT residuals
from the definitions for all $\bfPbNFits$ AKDE fits of the main and control
runs reproduces the solver's own residuals to $10^{-13}$ and every saved
support, but stage one reached its relative tolerance of $10^{-8}$ in only
$\bfPbSOneTol\%$ of them (median residual $\bfPbSOneMed$) and stage two reached
$10^{-7}$ in $\bfPbSTwoTol\%$ (maximum $\bfPbSTwoMax$). An audit on
$\bfAuditNInstances$ development instances compared the deployed $500$-sweep
solve with a $5{,}000$-sweep solve and with a residual-space FISTA reference at
the cross-validated setting of each instance
(Figure~\ref{fig:bf-diagnostics}). The reference reached its own tolerance in
only $\bfAuditTolFistaMultiscaleAkde\%$ and
$\bfAuditTolFistaSingleScaleAkde\%$ of multiscale and single-scale instances,
so it is a second opinion rather than a certificate. Relative objective gaps
were below $10^{-3}$ everywhere, but the selected support depends on the
budget: the Jaccard overlap between the deployed and the reference support had
median $\bfAuditJaccardMedMultiscaleAkde$ (multiscale) and
$\bfAuditJaccardMedSingleScaleAkde$ (single-scale), and the ISE after refitting
on the reference support changed by at most
$\bfAuditIseMaxRelChangeMultiscaleAkde\%$ for the multiscale entry but by up
to $\bfAuditIseMaxRelChangeSingleScaleAkde\%$ in one single-scale instance
(median $\bfAuditIseMedRelChangeSingleScaleAkde\%$). The comparison between the
two AKDE variants is therefore a comparison between two implemented procedures
at their documented budgets; the single-scale entry is the more
budget-sensitive of the two, and neither result should be read as a property
of the exact minimiser of either objective.

